codex
Built a self-contained Track B generator using the paper’s Section 3 3-SAT reduction. The paper’s explicit king-grid and strong-product constructions were avoided because their certificates are directly formulaic. [Paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2303.06986)

Local results:

- G1–G9(c) all pass.
- Exact witness density: \(1/2^{29}\).
- Five attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Gaussian reference: 6,097 mean scalar operations.
- Compact route: at most 153 operations.
- Answer: 10 serialized characters, 29 semantic bits.
- Independent BFS verification covers demo graphs.

Files:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2303.06986/gen_2303_06986.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2303.06986/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2303.06986/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2303.06986/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2303.06986/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2303.06986/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The result is not yet releasable: OpenRouter rejected every oracle call with HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded (total limit)`, so STEP 4 has no scored attempt. The transcripts retain those errors without treating them as model failures. Once quota is restored, rerun:

```bash
cd /home/gson/gvrepo/results/2303.06986
python3 ../../scripts/harden.py gen_2303_06986.py
```
