codex
Built and locally verified the Track B generator based on Theorem 3.1 and Claims 3.2–3.4 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2303.06986).

- All local G1–G9(c) gates pass at provisional `hard`: `n=53`, unique witness among `2^53` candidates, 0/200,000 guesses, five attacks at 0/8, and 273 intended operations.
- The oracle solved `easy` and `medium` 3/3 each.
- OpenRouter then exhausted its total key limit, so `hard` received no scored attempt. The result is therefore not yet shippable, and I did not create `REJECTED.md`.
- The README and transcripts record this blocker without treating HTTP errors as evidence of hardness.

Deliverables:

- [gen_2303_06986.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2303.06986/gen_2303_06986.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2303.06986/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2303.06986/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2303.06986/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2303.06986/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2303.06986/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

